{
  "quest.3B9F459FC8D63ED1.title": "&6Nitro Crystal",
  "quest.507466052C8963E2.quest_desc": [
    "&3Blazing Crystals&r are the Blazing tier. Each costs 120,000 FE in the orb, about a minute through one Starter rod.",
    "",
    "Blaze rods from a blaze farm are the easy supply. Keep spare crystals, because nine make a &3Blazing Crystal Block&r, which the Nitro tier and the Thermo Generator both use.",
  ],
  "quest.6E685D9B4F2E4835.title": "&aEnergized Steel",
  "quest.79BDC2AAA41B606C.quest_desc": [
    "The &2Magmator&r burns lava from its tank. Fill it with buckets or pipe lava in.",
    "",
    "It produces the same FE/t as a &aFurnator&r of the same tier. Every 100 mB of lava is worth 10,000 FE, so one bucket gives 100,000 FE at any tier.",
    "",
    "A pump on a Nether lava lake keeps it running without you.",
  ],
  "quest.5CB388F2A9A65BD6.quest_desc": [
    "&3Niotic Crystals&r cost 300,000 FE each in the orb.",
    "",
    "Niotic is where the reactor starts to pay off. A Niotic Reactor is rated at 2,560 FE/t, five times the Blazing one.",
  ],
  "task.5716EAED77C9E773.title": "Any Thermo Generator",
  "quest.2F3881EC8494FD41.title": "&aSolar Panel",
  "quest.11F7C5E1968C6302.title": "&3Thermo Generator",
  "quest.62DE7CEA9938DAE3.quest_desc": [
    "Point an &aEnergy Hopper&r into a chest or any other inventory and it charges the FE items inside it.",
    "",
    "Leave tools, armor and batteries in a chest next to it and they are full when you come back.",
  ],
  "quest.5A173AB935AC82E4.title": "&aFurnator",
  "task.191F5DB927BE118D.title": "Any Energy Hopper",
  "quest.6D4094356ADE50C1.quest_desc": [
    "Every reactor tier above Hardened is an upgrade of the one below. Each craft turns four blocks into four of the next tier, so a whole reactor takes nine crafts.",
    "",
    "Break your Hardened Reactor to get its blocks back, upgrade them and place it again. A Blazing Reactor is rated at 512 FE/t.",
  ],
  "quest.659B9311FB49C425.title": "&bPowah!",
  "task.57B0EC0DEAAB280A.title": "Any Furnator",
  "task.50E5F6B7D0E194CF.title": "Any Hardened or Better Rod",
  "quest.5CB388F2A9A65BD6.title": "&3Niotic Crystal",
  "quest.3D5E93A70A19DBEC.title": "&aFirst Generators",
  "quest.32AB4B67D179B660.title": "&6Heat Sources",
  "quest.4511A1FF62CE1D31.title": "&dSpirited Crystal",
  "quest.2ECA0F51EB4FEAF8.quest_desc": [
    "A Spirited Reactor is rated at 12,800 FE/t.",
    "",
    "Turn on auto mode in its screen and it stops when its buffer is full, then starts again once the buffer drops to 70%. That saves fuel whenever nothing is drawing the power.",
  ],
  "quest.4C85D0D1C8143B30.quest_desc": [
    "The top of &ePowah&r. A Nitro Reactor is rated at 64,000 FE/t from a 3 by 3 footprint.",
    "",
    "Its 36 blocks need 36 &6Nitro Capacitors&r, which is 144 Nitro Crystals, or nine Nether Stars.",
  ],
  "quest.2F3881EC8494FD41.quest_desc": [
    "A &aSolar Panel&r produces FE during the day with no fuel. It needs open sky above it, and it stops at night and in dimensions without daylight.",
    "",
    "It produces 8 FE/t at Starter and twice as much at each tier after that, up to 256 at Spirited, then 1,024 at Nitro.",
    "",
    "Panels are cheap for their output, so a roof of them is an easy way to cover a base's standby draw.",
  ],
  "quest.1E67AF1C79BF7DAE.quest_desc": [
    "The &ePowah&r &aWrench&r has three modes. Sneak + Right-click the air to switch between them.",
    "",
    "- &aConfig&r: sets which sides of a cable push or pull power.",
    "- &aLink&r: links blocks that pair up, such as the Energizing Orb and its rods.",
    "- &aRotate&r: turns generators and the orb to face another way.",
  ],
  "quest.32FD0431069FEC7F.quest_desc": [
    "A &dCharged Snowball&r calls down a lightning bolt wherever it hits.",
    "",
    "Lightning charges creepers, and a charged creeper killed by a player drops &eReliquary&r's &dEye of the Storm&r.",
  ],
  "quest.3B9F459FC8D63ED1.quest_desc": [
    "One energizing run makes sixteen &6Nitro Crystals&r and costs 20,000,000 FE. Through a single Hardened rod that takes over a quarter of an hour, so build faster rods and the generators to feed them first.",
    "",
    "Each run uses a Nether Star, and every Nitro block needs several crystals. A full Nitro Reactor alone takes nine stars.",
  ],
  "quest.3CAB1D7E7E1232A4.quest_desc": [
    "A Niotic Reactor is rated at 2,560 FE/t.",
    "",
    "Higher tiers also burn Uraninite faster, and a hot reactor burns it faster still, so good cooling saves fuel as well as raising output.",
  ],
  "quest.2CB16626FAB64712.quest_desc": [
    "&aUraninite&r fuels the reactor and goes into every reactor block.",
    "",
    "Its ore generates in the Overworld in three grades. Poor ore is found below y 64, regular below y 20 and Dense below y 0. The ore drops &aRaw Uraninite&r, which you can smelt, or energize for two Uraninite each.",
    "",
    "Stock up. A reactor is 36 blocks, and building a Hardened one takes 36 Uraninite before any fuel.",
  ],
  "quest.4BCFBAC4CF524BF2.title": "&bDry Ice",
  "quest.1E67AF1C79BF7DAE.title": "&aThe Wrench",
  "quest.6E685D9B4F2E4835.quest_desc": [
    "Every tier from Hardened up is made in the &aEnergizing Orb&r. Put the ingredients in the orb, and powered &aEnergizing Rods&r within 4 blocks of it send FE into them until the recipe finishes. The orb itself takes no power.",
    "",
    "&aEnergized Steel&r is the first recipe to make there. It goes into &aHardened Capacitors&r, and those go into the Hardened tier of every block.",
    "",
    "The Logistics chapter covers building the orb and its rods.",
  ],
  "quest.5A173AB935AC82E4.quest_desc": [
    "The &aFurnator&r burns anything a furnace burns. Every tier gets the same energy from a piece of fuel, 30 FE per tick of burn time, so one coal is worth 48,000 FE. Higher tiers burn it faster.",
    "",
    "It produces 16 FE/t at Starter, 64 at Basic and 128 at Hardened, doubling each tier after that to 1,024 at Spirited and 4,096 at Nitro.",
  ],
  "quest.507466052C8963E2.title": "&3Blazing Crystal",
  "quest.2CB16626FAB64712.title": "&aUraninite",
  "quest.3D5E93A70A19DBEC.quest_desc": [
    "Three generators work from the Starter tier, so build one of these first.",
    "",
    "- &aFurnator&r: burns furnace fuel.",
    "- &2Magmator&r: burns lava.",
    "- &aSolar Panel&r: runs on daylight.",
    "",
    "Each one needs a &aDielectric Casing&r. So does almost every other block in the mod, so make them in batches.",
  ],
  "quest.11F7C5E1968C6302.quest_desc": [
    "The &3Thermo Generator&r sits on a hot block and needs &bIndustrial Coolant&r in its tank, using 1 mB every two seconds.",
    "",
    "&cIn this pack it starts at Hardened.&r There is no Starter or Basic version, and the Hardened one takes a &aMagma Block&r in place of the Basic generator. You need &aHardened Capacitors&r from the energizing quest path first.",
    "",
    "With lava under it, it is rated at 64 FE/t at Hardened, up to 2,048 at Nitro. Hotter blocks raise that.",
  ],
  "quest.3CAB1D7E7E1232A4.title": "&3Niotic Reactor",
  "quest.79BDC2AAA41B606C.title": "&2Magmator",
  "quest.4BCFBAC4CF524BF2.quest_desc": [
    "&bDry Ice&r is one of the best solid coolants for the reactor, and in this pack it also makes the only liquid coolant.",
    "",
    "It generates underground below y 64 in icy biomes, or you can energize two &aBlue Ice&r into one for 10,000 FE.",
    "",
    "Drop a Dry Ice onto a water source block and that block becomes &bIndustrial Coolant&r, the only fluid the Reactor and Thermo Generator accept. The Power chapter's Keeping It Cool quest covers it in full.",
  ],
  "quest.659B9311FB49C425.quest_desc": [
    "&ePowah&r is a tiered FE mod with generators, energy storage and the crystals that connect the tiers. Nearly every block in it is a &aDielectric Casing&r and a &2Capacitor&r of the right tier, held together with Dielectric Paste.",
    "",
    "Blocks come in seven tiers, Starter, Basic, Hardened, Blazing, Niotic, Spirited and Nitro. Each tier is crafted from the one below plus that tier's capacitor, and from Hardened up those capacitors need a material made in the &aEnergizing Orb&r.",
    "",
    "&cThis pack changes a few things.&r The Reactor and Thermo Generator start at Hardened with their own recipes, and water no longer cools anything. The quests below explain each change where you meet it.",
    "",
    "Cables, energy cells and the orb itself are in the Logistics chapter, linked on the left.",
  ],
  "quest.32FD0431069FEC7F.title": "&dCharged Snowball",
  "quest.2ECA0F51EB4FEAF8.title": "&dSpirited Reactor",
  "quest.43504ED5CA8F70A6.title": "&3Faster Rods",
  "quest.4C85D0D1C8143B30.title": "&6Nitro Reactor",
  "quest.64DC0D2E2E556BC1.quest_desc": [
    "The &aReactor&r is a 36-block multiblock. Hold all 36 blocks and place one where a 3 by 3 area, 4 blocks tall, is clear, and it builds the rest itself. Breaking any part drops the whole reactor back as 36 blocks.",
    "",
    "&cIn this pack reactors start at Hardened.&r There is no Starter or Basic reactor, and Hardened blocks are crafted directly from Uraninite, &aHardened Capacitors&r and a &2Dielectric Casing&r.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Uraninite goes in the fuel slot. Three more things decide its output.",
    "",
    "- &aFuel level&r: output scales with how full the fuel gauge is, so keep it topped up.",
    "- &aCarbon and redstone&r: any furnace fuel in the carbon slot and redstone in the redstone slot together raise output by about two thirds, but they also heat the reactor.",
    "- &bCoolant&r: heat cuts output. Keep &bIndustrial Coolant&r in the tank and ice or &bDry Ice&r in the solid coolant slot. The solid coolant only works while the tank has coolant in it.",
    "",
    "Cooled properly, a Hardened Reactor runs close to its 128 FE/t rating.",
  ],
  "task.3A5A512C7164CE80.title": "Any Magmator",
  "task.55B90D46974B9F90.title": "Any Energy Discharger",
  "quest.43504ED5CA8F70A6.quest_desc": [
    "Each &aEnergizing Rod&r sends a fixed amount into the orb per tick. It is 100 FE/t at Starter, 400 at Basic, 1,000 at Hardened, 4,000 at Blazing, 10,000 at Niotic, 40,000 at Spirited and 200,000 at Nitro. Every powered rod in range adds to the total.",
    "",
    "Rods only work as fast as they are fed. A ring of Nitro rods on one small generator is no faster than the generator.",
  ],
  "quest.32AB4B67D179B660.quest_desc": [
    "A Thermo Generator's output scales with the heat of the block under it. Lava counts as 1,000, a &aMagma Block&r as 800 and a &3Blazing Crystal Block&r as 1,500. JEI's Heat Sources page lists the rest.",
    "",
    "This pack adds three much hotter ones. The &dEclipse Ember Block&r from &eJust Dire Things&r is 3,000, and &eOritech&r's &5Manhattan Module&r and the Nuke from &eIndustrial Contraptions&r are 4,000 each.",
    "",
    "A Nitro Thermo Generator on a Manhattan Module produces 8,192 FE/t.",
  ],
  "quest.1F9BB436BA7661B2.title": "&aEnergy Discharger",
  "quest.64DC0D2E2E556BC1.title": "&aHardened Reactor",
  "quest.6D4094356ADE50C1.title": "&3Blazing Reactor",
  "quest.62DE7CEA9938DAE3.title": "&aEnergy Hopper",
  "task.7CAAE738E0F25FC5.title": "Any Solar Panel",
  "quest.4511A1FF62CE1D31.quest_desc": [
    "&dSpirited Crystals&r cost 1,000,000 FE each. One Hardened rod takes 50 seconds per crystal and one Blazing rod about 12, so this is the point where better rods save real time.",
    "",
    "They use emeralds, and villager trading is the steadiest source.",
  ],
  "quest.1F9BB436BA7661B2.quest_desc": [
    "The &aEnergy Discharger&r does the opposite. It drains FE out of items placed in it into its own buffer, and cables can pull that power out.",
    "",
    "Use it to empty spare batteries back into your network.",
  ],
}